<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Hospitaller Rhodes</h1><p class="st-meta">1310 CE – 1522 CE · capital Rhodes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Rhodes under the Knights Hospitaller, a crusading order-state that held out against Mamluks and Ottomans for two centuries before Suleiman took it in 1522.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> in 1291 the Knights of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Order of Saint John</a> moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>. Seeking a base of their own, Grand Master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/foulques-de-villaret">Foulques de Villaret</a> attacked Byzantine <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rhodes">Rhodes</a> in 1306, and the city fell in 1309-1310. The order also took nearby islands and later built the castle of Saint Peter at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/halicarnassus">Bodrum</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Grand Master and a council of knights, organised by national langues, governed a Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> population and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> settlers. The order ran a hospital, built great walls and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palace-of-the-grand-master-rhodes">Palace of the Grand Master</a>, and used its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galley">galleys</a> against Muslim shipping. It acquired much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Templars</a>' wealth after 1312. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-daubusson">Pierre d'Aubusson</a> it repulsed the Ottoman siege of 1480.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1522 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> besieged <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rhodes">Rhodes</a> with a vast army. After six months Grand Master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippe-villiers-de-lisle-adam">Philippe Villiers de l'Isle-Adam</a> surrendered on honourable terms, and the knights left in early 1523, settling in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a> in 1530. Their medieval city is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/hospitaller-rhodes.jpg" alt="Hospitaller Rhodes" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Order_of_St._John_(various).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1310 CE – 1522 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rhodes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Foulques de Villaret, Pierre d'Aubusson, Philippe Villiers de l'Isle-Adam</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity (rulers), Eastern Orthodox Christianity (population)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French, Italian, Latin, Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rhodes under the Knights Hospitaller, Knights of Rhodes</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1416&amp;focus=hospitaller-rhodes" aria-label="Hospitaller Rhodes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5390 864 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hospitaller Rhodes lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5710 1120L5675 1054M5710 1120L5709 970M5710 1120L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5675 1054h0M5709 970h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5710 1120h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5710 1120h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Rhodes. <a href="/atlas?year=1416&amp;focus=hospitaller-rhodes">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

